## 2026-10-01 — Progressive loading bar + clustered coalition members
- index.html: splash now has a real progress bar with "About N seconds left". Estimate = how long recent loads took (localStorage openthink.loadMs, default 6 s), moving steadily to 90% by then and creeping after; sharpened by real progress from main.ts (fetch start, streamed download when content-length is known, drawing, tabs). Animation: canvas bubbles that grow and split; how many may exist follows the progress. Reduced-motion: static redraw only.
- graph.ts coalition zoom: members packed into staggered rows on an oval around the items (wider than tall, since item labels run sideways), bigger orgs on inner rows; zoom fit uses the oval. Replaces the single huge ring.
- Tested in Playwright with data slowed 7 s: bar 15% / 44% / 73% at 1 / 3 / 5 s with 5 / 4 / 2 s left; Mass Power Forward zoom shows 104 members in ~4 rows, no page errors.
- Uncertainty: the first visit on a device has no history, so the countdown starts from the 6 s guess; the Apps Script feed sends no content-length, so there the bar is time-based.
